WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.930
From a Breaking Bad movie to a brand new Stephen
King adaptation, there are some great new

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.990
Netflix originals landing on the streaming
service next month.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.249
Let's take a look at everything good coming
to Netflix in October 2019.

00:00:11.249 --> 00:00:12.730
In the Tall Grass

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:16.250
Nobody needs a reminder of the Stephen King
revival that's happening right now, but fewer

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.570
people are aware that King's son, who writes
under the name Joe Hill, is also becoming

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.529
a name to know in the horror world.

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:28.289
Hill's 2007 novel Horns was adapted into a
film starring Daniel Radcliffe in 2014, and

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:33.190
his third novel, NOS4A2, was recently adapted
into a series on AMC that looks downright

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:34.190
terrifying.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:38.239
So what kind of epic premise could they concoct
when they work on a story together?

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:42.070
In the Tall Grass is one of those premises
that only a King could come up with, and only

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:43.609
a King could pull off.

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:47.210
The film, like the story, follows a pregnant
woman and her brother who enter a field of

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.210
deadly grass after they hear a child crying
for help.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:54.140
What follows next is the kind of terror that
takes root and doesn't let go.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.899
You can get your chloro-fill when In the Tall
Grass hits Netflix on October 4th.

00:00:57.899 --> 00:00:58.960
Big Mouth: Season 3

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.679
For two seasons now, Big Mouth has proven
itself to be one of the raunchiest animated

00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:06.390
shows available, following the adventures
of a bunch of school-age children as they

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:07.550
go through puberty.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:11.600
But underneath the crude humor and poop jokes,
you'll find a lot of heart in this show.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.760
Creators Nick Kroll, Andrew Goldberg, Jennifer
Flackett, and Mark Levin are returning next

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.390
month with a brand new season, which you'll
be able to stream on October 4th.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.390
El Camino: A Breaking Bad Movie

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.500
As far as series finales go, Breaking Bad
wrapped up its final season with a bow, tying

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:29.170
together nearly every dangling plot thread
in a breathtaking final few episodes and closing

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:32.530
out on Walter White himself sprawled dead
in a meth lab.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:33.930
So what's left to tell?

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:37.700
Why would creator Vince Gilligan return six
years later to rip off that bow?

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.220
One word:

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.000
"Jesse."

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:45.390
The last we saw of Jesse, he was driving off
into the night, cackling like a lunatic, finally

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.730
freed from those crazy white supremacists.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:48.910
Where does he go from there?

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:52.670
Remember, this is a guy who recently found
out that his partner watched one of his girlfriends

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.710
overdose and did nothing to stop it.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.090
Then he watched someone execute his other
girlfriend, leaving behind a young boy for

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.510
whom he cares deeply.

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:02.430
He's going to be carrying a lot of emotions
in this new outing.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.830
Strap in when El Camino: A Breaking Bad Movie
roars onto Netflix on October 11th.

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:07.830
Fractured

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.739
The horror continues later this October with
Fractured, a tense psychological thriller

00:02:11.739 --> 00:02:14.299
featuring Sam Worthington and Lily Rabe.

00:02:14.299 --> 00:02:18.049
Worthington stars as a loving father who goes
on the hunt for his daughter and wife after

00:02:18.049 --> 00:02:20.540
they vanish from a hospital emergency room.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.349
The more he searches, the more he begins to
suspect that the hospital itself may have

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:26.879
something to do with the chilling disappearances.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:31.290
From the sounds of it, Fractured is going
to be chock full of fun, guns, and Sam Worthingtons,

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.890
and you can experience the wild ride on October
11th.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:35.049
Haunted: Season 2

00:02:35.049 --> 00:02:39.110
It's the month for all things horror, so it
stands to reason that Netflix would be doubling

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:40.489
down on its scares.

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:44.749
If you missed the first season of Haunted
when it dropped in 2018, here's the basic

00:02:44.749 --> 00:02:48.299
premise: People who have had real paranormal
encounters meet with the show's producers

00:02:48.299 --> 00:02:52.810
and discuss their experiences, while reenactments
play out along with their stories.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:56.810
Look for Haunted: Season 2 to scare the living
daylights out of you on October 11th.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:57.810
The Laundromat

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:02.540
There's a ton of talent packed into The Laundromat,
a biographical film about a shady law firm

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.269
located in Panama that spent years helping
some of the world's richest people launder

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:07.269
their money.

00:03:07.269 --> 00:03:11.730
Academy Award winners Meryl Streep and Gary
Oldman share screentime with Antonio Banderas

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.120
in this off-the-wall comedy directed by Steven
Soderbergh.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.519
After her husband drowns, elderly Ellen Martin,
played by Streep, finds herself inadvertently

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:22.299
on the trail of a widespread insurance fraud
scheme.

00:03:22.299 --> 00:03:25.930
Forget about all that real laundry you promised
yourself you'd do, and take a look at The

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.069
Laundromat when it opens on October 18.

00:03:28.069 --> 00:03:29.150
Living with Yourself

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.700
It's a fact: Paul Rudd makes everything better.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:36.280
From Ant-Man to Celery Man, Rudd brings depth,
charm, and humor to nearly every character

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.280
he touches.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.300
This guy would never hurt a fly.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.240
"You're welcome."

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.740
In fact, the only thing better than one Rudd
is two Rudds, which is why you should definitely

00:03:49.749 --> 00:03:51.630
watch Living With Yourself.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.610
In Living With Yourself, Paul Rudd pulls double
duty as a corporate loser just trying to get

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:59.950
through the day to day grind, and as a better,
funnier, smarter version of himself that emerges

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.560
after he undergoes a mysterious spa treatment.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:07.129
The official trailer teases a show that looks
both hilarious and surprisingly creepy.

00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:08.799
Look for it on October 18.

00:04:08.799 --> 00:04:09.799
Daybreak

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:12.719
What would you do if you were one of the last
survivors of the apocalypse?

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:16.650
As Netflix sees it, you'd either blindfold
yourself, keep really quiet, team up with

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:20.160
some local high school gangs, take a road
trip with your father in law, get out of the

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.060
rain, or just cry a lot.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.850
But what's to say you couldn't enjoy that
apocalypse?

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:29.730
In Daybreak, a nuclear explosion near the
town of Glendale turns the area into a wasteland,

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.950
but that won't stop one teen from living life
to the fullest.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:37.420
The trailer promises a Ferris Bueller-style,
fourth-wall-breaking romp - up to and including

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.760
Bueller himself, Matthew Broderick.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.760
Take a look when Daybreak arrives on Netflix
on October 24.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.940
Dolemite Is My Name

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:48.040
Back in the '70s, comedian Rudy Ray Moore
created a fictional persona that he named

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:52.830
Dolemite He went on to make a series of exploitation
films based around that character, and went

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:53.960
down in history.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:58.560
Who better to play this loud-talking, swaggering
cinematic hero than Eddie Murphy, who steps

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.430
into the role of Moore with what critics are
calling "feisty glee."

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:06.750
Wesley Snipes and Keegan-Michael Key costar,
and if you're looking for an absolutely wild

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:10.200
movie night this October, you can stream Dolemite
is My Name on the 25th.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.450
Original stand-up comedy

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.680
As we wind down the Netflix originals, we
have to give a shout-out to some of the new

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.490
stand-up comedies hitting small screens next
month.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:21.730
On the first, you'll get front-row seats to
Nikki Glaser: Bangin', an irreverent stand-up

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:25.090
set that sees the comic covering everything
from sex to careers.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:29.460
On the eighth, look for Deon Cole to take
the stage with Cole Hearted, followed by Jenny

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.270
Slate: Stage Fright on the 22nd.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:35.721
Finally, the month will end on a high note
with a brand new set from Arsenio Hall, Smart

00:05:35.721 --> 00:05:38.290
&amp; Classy, on October 29.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:41.940
That does it for all the fantastic new Netflix
originals to look for in October.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.720
Now let's see what other movies will be worth
staying up for.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:45.720
New movies

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.030
Netflix's upcoming action films are as diverse
as they are explosive.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:53.610
October first sees the glut of the new arrivals,
with both Charlie's Angels films, Men in Black

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:56.660
II, The Island, and Troy hitting the service
all at once.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:06:01.430
You can also rewatch both Bad Boys films in
anticipation of 2020's Bad Boys for Life,

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:05.100
which reunites Will Smith and Martin Lawrence
as the iconic buddy cop duo.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:09.480
After that, you'll be able to catch the first
Men in Black on October 19th, as well as Master

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:12.070
Z: The Ip Man Legacy on the 23rd.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.070
That's a sweet lineup.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:14.900
"Edgar what on Earth was that?"

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:15.900
"Sugar."

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.940
''Never seen sugar do that."

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:23.180
It wouldn't be October without some new scares,
and Netflix is stepping up to the plate.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:28.060
The first of the month marks the arrival of
1997's horror satire Scream 2, as well as

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.350
2016's Sinister Circle.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:34.510
You should also keep an eye out for A.M.I.,
an indie screamer about an artificial intelligence

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:37.920
in a girl's phone that convinces her to start
taking lives.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.840
Like the action genre, most of the month's
drama additions land at the opening of the

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:42.840
month.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:46.430
You'll start seeing some all-time greats in
your browsing options, including Blow, Crash,

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:48.540
Sin City, The Bucket List, and Trainspotting.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:53.200
We're also getting Ocean's Twelve and Thirteen,
No Reservations, and the Will Smith tearjerker

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.900
The Pursuit of Happyness.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:58.600
Later in the month, don't miss Dark Crimes,
starring Jim Carrey way against type as a

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:02.040
hardboiled detective on the hunt for a cold-blooded
murderer.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:06.150
And on the 31st, you can't miss Martin Scorsese's
classic Raging Bull.

